                    [
                      "_text",
                      "## Overlaps<br>\u2014<br>{b}object|what it is instead<br>`clip~`|the same job as `pong~ @mode clip` in its own box. Its one extra is `@mode Zero` which outputs 0 outside the bounds instead of the bound itself.<br>tab 3's signal maths|`tanh~` and the rest are the smooth versions of the same idea. They never have a corner.<br>`deltaclip~`|limits how fast a signal may change rather than how loud it may get<br>`phasewrap~`|`pong~ @mode wrap` fixed at +pi and -pi. For phase arithmetic rather than timbre.<br>`lookup~` on tab 4|can imitate any of these and anything else with a drawn curve<br>`round~`|quantises amplitude to a step rather than bounding it<br>\u2014<br><br>## Packages<br>\u2014<br>{b}package|what it adds<br>**ableton-dsp** *ships inside Max*|`abl.dsp.saturator~` `abl.dsp.overdrive~` `abl.dsp.distortion~` `abl.dsp.fuzz~` `abl.dsp.expshaper~` `abl.device.roar~` \u2014 voiced effect units rather than primitives. `patches/shootouts/distortion-shootout.maxpat` auditions eighteen of them.<br>**ableton-dsp** *ships inside Max*|`abl.dsp.waveshaper~` \u2014 tab 6<br>**s2n**|`sn.drive~` \u2014 tab 6<br>**PeRColate**|`flip~` folds around a threshold and its own help file says `pong~` superseded it \u00b7 `weave~` flips a square wave after counted zero crossings for subharmonics<br>**TS.Modular**|`ts.wavefolder` `ts.saturation` `ts.overdrive`<br>**BEAP** *ships inside Max*|`bp.Wavefolder` `bp.Folder` \u2014 several folding stages \u00b7 Paste From > BEAP<br>**ears**|`ears.clip~` `ears.overdrive~` \u2014 the same jobs offline on a buffer<br>\u2014"
                    ],
                    [
                      "_wrap",
                      1
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              },
