       \"presentation\": [\n              20,\n              902,\n              1100,\n              376\n            ],\n            \"attrs\": {\n              \"fontname\": \"Monaco\",\n              \"border\": 0,\n              \"textcolor\": [\n                0.68,\n                0.7,\n                0.74,\n                1.0\n              ],\n              \"filename\": \"butter_comment.js\",\n              \"fontsize\": 10.0\n            },\n            \"inlets\": 1,\n            \"outlets\": 2,\n            \"outlettype\": [\n              \"\",\n              \"\"\n            ],\n            \"box_extras\": {\n              \"embedstate\": [\n                [\n                  \"bgcolor\",\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubble\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubble_bgcolor\",\n                  1,\n                  1,\n                  1,\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubble_outlinecolor\",\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubblepoint\",\n                  0.5\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubbleside\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubbletextmargin\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubbleusescolors\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"underline\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_autoheight\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_bullet\",\n                  \"\\u2022\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_codebg\",\n                  0.0,\n                  0.0,\n                  0.0,\n                  0.18\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_headingscale\",\n                  0.75\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_hyperlinkcolor\",\n                  0.2,\n                  0.45,\n                  0.95,\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_indent\",\n                  14\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_linespacing\",\n                  1.2\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_linkunderline\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_markdown\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_monofont\",\n                  \"\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_padding\",\n                  8\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_paraspacing\",\n                  0.5\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_pointsize\",\n                  12,\n                  10\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_sendto\",\n                  \"\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablecolor\",\n                  0.45,\n                  0.46,\n                  0.5,\n                  0.7\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablefill\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablepad\",\n                  4\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablewrap\",\n                  0.3\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_text\",\n                  \"## Overlaps<br>\\u2014<br>{b}object|what it is instead<br>`clip~`|the same job as `pong~ @mode clip` in its own box. Its one extra is `@mode Zero` which outputs 0 outside the bounds instead of the bound itself.<br>tab 3's signal maths|`tanh~` and the rest are the smooth versions of the same idea. They never have a corner.<br>`deltaclip~`|limits how fast a signal may change rather than how loud it may get<br>`phasewrap~`|`pong~ @mode wrap` fixed at +pi and -pi. For phase arithmetic rather than timbre.<br>`lookup~` on tab 4|can imitate any of these and anything else with a drawn curve<br>`round~`|quantises amplitude to a step rather than bounding it<br>\\u2014<br><br>## Packages<br>\\u2014<br>{b}package|what it adds<br>**ableton-dsp** *ships inside Max*|`abl.dsp.saturator~` `abl.dsp.overdrive~` `abl.dsp.distortion~` `abl.dsp.fuzz~` `abl.dsp.expshaper~` `abl.device.roar~` \\u2014 voiced effect units rather than primitives. `patches/shootouts/distortion-shootout.maxpat` auditions eighteen of them.<br>**ableton-dsp** *ships inside Max*|`abl.dsp.waveshaper~` \\u2014 tab 6<br>**s2n**|`sn.drive~` \\u2014 tab 6<br>**PeRColate**|`flip~` folds around a threshold and its own help file says `pong~` superseded it \\u00b7 `weave~` flips a square wave after counted zero crossings for subharmonics<br>**TS.Modular**|`ts.wavefolder` `ts.saturation` `ts.overdrive`<br>**BEAP** *ships inside Max*|`bp.Wavefolder` `bp.Folder` \\u2014 several folding stages \\u00b7 Paste From > BEAP<br>**ears**|`ears.clip~` `ears.overdrive~` \\u2014 the same jobs offline on a buffer<br>\\u2014\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_wrap\",\n                  1\n                ]\n              ]\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"connections\": [\n          [\n            \"gain_init\",\n            0,\n            \"gain\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"src_in\",\n            0,\n            \"drive\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gain\",\n            0,\n            \"drive\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"od_init\",\n            0,\n            \"od\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"drive\",\n            0,\n            \"soft\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"soft\",\n            0,\n            \"sel\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pmode_ui\",\n            0,\n            \"fold\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prange_ui\",\n            0,\n            \"fold\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"drive\",\n            0,\n            \"fold\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"fold\",\n            0,\n            \"sel\",\n            2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"which\",\n            0,\n            \"rt_t\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rt_t\",\n            1,\n            \"rt_off\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rt_t\",\n            0,\n            \"sel_plus\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rt_off\",\n            0,\n            \"rt_del\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rt_del\",\n            0,\n            \"rt_on\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rt_off\",\n            0,\n            \"scope\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"rt_on\",\n            0,\n            \"scope\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sel_plus\",\n            0,\n            \"sel\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sel\",\n            0,\n            \"scope\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"src_in\",\n            0,\n            \"scope\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gate_tog\",\n            0,\n            \"gate_msg\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gate_msg\",\n            0,\n            \"gate_line\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gate_line\",\n            0,\n            \"gate_mul\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sel\",\n            0,\n            \"gate_mul\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gate_mul\",\n            0,\n            \"send_l\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gate_mul\",\n            0,\n            \"send_r\",\n            0\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"patcher_extras\": {\n          \"showontab\": 1\n        }\n      },\n      \"box_extras\": {\n        \"comment\": \"no inlets or outlets \\u2014 this subpatcher is a tab of the window; it reaches the master output through s~ REF_L / s~ REF_R\",\n        \"saved_object_attributes\": {\n          \"description\": \"\",\n          \"digest\": \"\",\n          \"globalpatchername\": \"\",\n          \"tags\": \"\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tab_math\": {\n      \"type\": \"newobj\",\n      \"text\": \"p \\\"3 signal maths\\\"\",\n      \"pos\": [\n        620,\n        468\n      ],\n      \"inlets\": 0,\n      \"outlets\": 0,\n      \"outlettype\": [],\n      \"attrs\": {\n        \"comment\": \"no inlets or outlets \\u2014 this subpatcher is a tab of the window; it reaches the master output through s~ REF_L / s~ REF_R\"\n      },\n      \"patcher\": {\n        \"width\": 1160,\n        \"height\": 2720,\n        \"bglocked\": 1,\n        \"objects\": {\n          \"header\": {\n            \"type\": \"comment\",\n            \"text\": \"3 \\u00b7 Signal maths \\u2014 the one-in one-out objects used as transfer functions\",\n            \"pos\": [\n              20,\n              14\n            ],\n            \"size\": [\n              1100,\n              24\n            ],\n            \"presentation\": [\n              20,\n              14,\n              1100,\n              24\n            ],\n            \"attrs\": {\n              \"fontname\": \"Monaco\",\n              \"fontsize\": 13.0,\n              \"fontface\": 1,\n              \"textcolor\": [\n                1.0,\n                0.55,\n                0.0,\n                1.0\n              ]\n            },\n            \"inlets\": 1,\n            \"outlets\": 0,\n            \"outlettype\": []\n          },\n          \"blurb\": {\n            \"type\": \"comment\",\n            \"text\": \"Every object here takes a signal and returns a number computed from it, sample by sample.  That is the whole definition of a waveshaper, which is why this page and tab 4's lookup~ are the same idea twice: these are curves Max already knows, lookup~ is a curve you draw.  Not one of them has an attribute \\u2014 the drive above is the only control, and how hard you push decides which part of the curve the signal visits.  A clip~ -1. 1. sits after the selector because tanx~ and atanh~ will happily send several thousand at full drive.\",\n            \"pos\": [\n              20,\n              44\n            ],\n            \"size\": [\n              1100,\n              51\n            ],\n            \"presentation\": [\n              20,\n              44,\n              1100,\n              52\n            ],\n            \"attrs\": {\n              \"fontname\": \"Monaco\",\n              \"fontsize\": 10.0,\n              \"textcolor\": [\n                0.9,\n                0.9,\n                0.92,\n                1.0\n              ],\n              \"presentation_linecount\": 3\n            },\n            \"inlets\": 1,\n            \"outlets\": 0,\n            \"outlettype\": []\n          },\n          \"src_in\": {\n            \"type\": \"newobj\",\n            \"text\": \"r~ SRC\",\n            \"pos\": [\n              20,\n              140\n            ],\n            \"inlets\": 1,\n            \"outlets\": 1,\n            \"outlettype\": [\n              \"\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"b0_title\": {\n            \"type\": \"comment\",\n            \"text\": \"drive \\u2014 the only control a nonlinearity has\",\n            \"pos\": [\n      