\n            \"size\": [\n              1100,\n              281\n            ],\n            \"presentation\": [\n              20,\n              994,\n              1100,\n              281\n            ],\n            \"attrs\": {\n              \"fontname\": \"Monaco\",\n              \"border\": 0,\n              \"textcolor\": [\n                0.68,\n                0.7,\n                0.74,\n                1.0\n              ],\n              \"filename\": \"butter_comment.js\",\n              \"fontsize\": 10.0\n            },\n            \"inlets\": 1,\n            \"outlets\": 2,\n            \"outlettype\": [\n              \"\",\n              \"\"\n            ],\n            \"box_extras\": {\n              \"embedstate\": [\n                [\n                  \"bgcolor\",\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubble\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubble_bgcolor\",\n                  1,\n                  1,\n                  1,\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubble_outlinecolor\",\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  0,\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubblepoint\",\n                  0.5\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubbleside\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubbletextmargin\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"bubbleusescolors\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"underline\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_autoheight\",\n                  0\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_bullet\",\n                  \"\\u2022\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_codebg\",\n                  0.0,\n                  0.0,\n                  0.0,\n                  0.18\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_headingscale\",\n                  0.75\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_hyperlinkcolor\",\n                  0.2,\n                  0.45,\n                  0.95,\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_indent\",\n                  14\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_linespacing\",\n                  1.2\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_linkunderline\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_markdown\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_monofont\",\n                  \"\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_padding\",\n                  8\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_paraspacing\",\n                  0.5\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_pointsize\",\n                  12,\n                  10\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_sendto\",\n                  \"\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablecolor\",\n                  0.45,\n                  0.46,\n                  0.5,\n                  0.7\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablefill\",\n                  1\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablepad\",\n                  4\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_tablewrap\",\n                  0.3\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_text\",\n                  \"## Overlaps<br>\\u2014<br>{b}object|what it is instead<br>`table~`|the same idea at integer indices into a `table` object rather than a `buffer~`<br>`clip~` `pong~` on tab 2|fixed curves this can imitate. And then some.<br>tab 3's signal maths|the curves Max already knows. This is the one you draw.<br>`peek~`|writes the curve a sample at a time when the patch has to compute it<br>`buffer~` `fill` and `apply`|the standard shapes without any computing. See tab 1's REFTABLE block.<br>\\u2014<br><br>## Packages<br>\\u2014<br>{b}package|what it adds<br>**PeRColate**|`gen17` solves Chebyshev polynomials into exactly this table so a full-level sine through it gains precisely the harmonics asked for. Wired on tab 6.<br>**TS.Modular**|`ts.waveshaper` \\u2014 a curve you draw by hand<br>**BEAP** *ships inside Max*|`bp.Waveshaper` `bp.Table` \\u00b7 Paste From > BEAP > Waveshapers<br>**ableton-dsp** *ships inside Max*|`abl.dsp.waveshaper~` on tab 6 builds its curve from parameters not a table<br>\\u2014\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_wrap\",\n                  1\n                ]\n              ]\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"connections\": [\n          [\n            \"gain_init\",\n            0,\n            \"gain\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"src_in\",\n            0,\n            \"drive\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gain\",\n            0,\n            \"drive\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lk_size\",\n            0,\n            \"look\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lk_off\",\n            0,\n            \"look\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lk_chan\",\n            0,\n            \"look\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"drive\",\n            0,\n            \"look\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lb\",\n            0,\n            \"lb_b\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lb_b\",\n            1,\n         