pshaper~`|one exponential curve and one `@amount`. The small version of the same idea.<br>`abl.dsp.saturator~`|Live's Saturator: fewer controls and a voiced result<br>`abl.device.roar~`|three saturation stages with routing between them<br>`Abl.Waveshaper~`|the panelled module wrapping the same DSP. It carries MC stereo cords.<br>`lookup~` on tab 4|the same job with a curve you supply instead of parameters<br>\\u2014<br><br>## Packages<br>\\u2014<br>{b}package|what it adds<br>**s2n**|`mc.sn.drive~` and `mcs.sn.drive~` are the multichannel forms of `sn.drive~`<br>**PeRColate**|`gen9` `gen10` `gen7` `gen5` `gen20` `gen24` `gen25` compute other table contents<br>**PeRColate**|`dcblock~` \\u2014 a waveshaper with an asymmetric curve generates DC. Block it.<br>**TS.Modular**|`ts.waveshaper` `ts.wavefolder` `ts.saturation` `ts.overdrive`<br>**PnP.Maxtools**|`pnp.distort~`<br>**Upshot**|`upshot_distortion` `upshot_waveshapedistortion`<br>\\u2014\"\n                ],\n                [\n                  \"_wrap\",\n                  1\n                ]\n              ]\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"connections\": [\n          [\n            \"gain_init\",\n            0,\n            \"gain\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"src_in\",\n            0,\n            \"drive\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gain\",\n            0,\n            \"drive\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ws_drive\",\n            0,\n            \"shaper\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ws_shdrive\",\n            0,\n            \"shaper\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ws_mix\",\n            0,\n            \"shaper\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ws_curve\",\n            0,\n            \"shaper\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ws_depth\",\n            0,\n            \"shaper\",\n         